/*  FUNCTION NAME:      BYDIAGONALS
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Applies a function (default CONCAT) to each ↘ diagonal of a grid, each ↙ anti-diagonal, or both, returning one result per diagonal as a column.*/
/*  REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-08-24  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-08-24  Claude      Boolean antidiagonal flag becomes numeric mode: 0 = diagonals, 1 = anti-diagonals, 2 = both in one pass
                        2026-08-24  Claude      fn may return an array, not just a scalar (like BIROW/BICOL): per-diagonal results are VSTACKed, so LAMBDA(d, d) flattens the grid diagonal-wise
*/
BYDIAGONALS = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [grid],
    [fn],
    [mode],
//  Help
    LET(Help, TEXTSPLIT(
                "FUNCTION:      →BYDIAGONALS(grid, [fn], [mode])¶" &
                "DESCRIPTION:   →Applies fn (default CONCAT) to each ↘ diagonal of grid, each ↙ anti-diagonal, or both, returning one result per diagonal as a column. The diagonal companion to BYROW/BYCOL.¶" &
                "VERSION:       →Aug 24 2026¶" &
                "PARAMETERS:    →¶" &
                "   grid          →(Required) A 2D array or range (e.g. a letter grid).¶" &
                "   fn            →(Optional) LAMBDA applied to each diagonal, received as a column read in the arrow direction. May return a scalar (one result per diagonal, like BYROW) or an array (per-diagonal results are stacked vertically, like BIROW - e.g. LAMBDA(d, d) flattens the grid diagonal-wise into one column; ragged widths pad with #N/A). Built-ins can be passed by name (e.g. SUM). Default CONCAT, so the default output is a column of diagonal strings.¶" &
                "   mode          →(Optional) (0) ↘ diagonals [default], listed from the bottom-left corner to the top-right corner, each read top-left to bottom-right - ROWS+COLUMNS-1 results; (1) ↙ anti-diagonals, listed from the top-left corner to the bottom-right corner, each read top-right to bottom-left; (2) both in one pass - the ↘ block stacked above the ↙ block, 2*(ROWS+COLUMNS-1) results.¶" &
                "EXAMPLE:       →¶" &
                "Formula        →=BYDIAGONALS({""A"",""B"";""C"",""D""})¶" &
                "Result         →{""C"";""AD"";""B""}",
                "→", "¶"
                ),
    //  Check inputs
        Help?, ISOMITTED(grid),
    //  Procedure
        nR, ROWS(grid),
        nC, COLUMNS(grid),
        op, IF(ISOMITTED(fn), CONCAT, fn),
        md, IF(ISOMITTED(mode), 0, N(mode)),
    //  Diagonal k of nR+nC-1: down-right family satisfies col-row = k-nR (k=1 at bottom-left);
    //  anti family satisfies row+col = k+1 (k=1 at top-left), read in the ↙ direction (row ascending)
    //  REDUCE + VSTACK (not MAKEARRAY) so fn may return an array per diagonal;
    //  the scalar 0 seed row is dropped after stacking
        family, LAMBDA(anti, DROP(REDUCE(0, SEQUENCE(nR + nC - 1), LAMBDA(acc, k,
                    VSTACK(acc, LET(
                        startRow, IF(anti, MAX(1, k + 1 - nC), MAX(1, nR - k + 1)),
                        endRow, IF(anti, MIN(nR, k), MIN(nR, nR + nC - k)),
                        rowsV, SEQUENCE(endRow - startRow + 1, 1, startRow),
                        colsV, IF(anti, k + 1 - rowsV, rowsV + k - nR),
                        op(INDEX(grid, rowsV, colsV)))))), 1)),
        result, IFS(md = 0, family(FALSE),
                    md = 1, family(TRUE),
                    md = 2, VSTACK(family(FALSE), family(TRUE))),
        IF(Help?, Help, result)
)
);
